meta {
  name: read-missing
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/archive-jobs/{{missingJobId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

tests {
  test("Declared HTTP status", function () { expect(res.status).to.equal(404); });
  test("Declared application code", function () { expect(res.body.error.code).to.equal("JOB_NOT_FOUND"); });
}

docs {
  Set missingJobId to a syntactically valid ID confirmed absent in the target test dataset. No absent ID is supplied.

  Evidence: normative synthetic contract demo-1. This request and its assertions have not been run.
  The example.test host is illustrative. Replace it only with an authorized test service. No login or refresh endpoint is defined.

  Declared response: HTTP 404 Not Found.
  Caller action: Verify the ID; do not retry blindly.

  Complete illustrative response. Message text is not a stable identifier.
  ```http
  HTTP/1.1 404 Not Found
  Content-Type: application/json
  X-Request-ID: req_demo_error

  {
    "error": {
      "code": "JOB_NOT_FOUND",
      "message": "No job has that ID."
    },
    "request_id": "req_demo_error"
  }
  ```
}
